# BEGIN superflow:fork
# Fork-owned files pinned merge=ours keep the fork's copy on upstream-port's release
# merge. The pin only works when that merge runs with -c merge.ours.driver=true: the
# key is deliberately NOT in git config (./.fork/setup.sh unsets it; ./.fork/setup.sh --check
# fails if it is set), so every other merge text-merges these paths like any file.
# A pin hides upstream's changes, so upstream-port reads upstream's diff of each pinned
# path by hand at every port; a rename/delete upstream still stops as modify/delete.
# Pin only whole files the fork owns, never a file with small inline edits (let those
# conflict so rerere can learn the fix). Globs work. ./.fork/check.sh fails if a
# pinned path matches no tracked file.
AGENTS.md merge=ours

# --- Syntax-aware merge via mergiraf (https://mergiraf.org) ---------------------
# A conservative AST merge driver that clears noise conflicts (reordered methods,
# import churn, formatting) and falls back to conflict markers when unsure. These
# lines are active once ./.fork/setup.sh registers the driver in the clone:
#   git config merge.mergiraf.driver 'mergiraf merge --git %O %A %B -s %S -x %X -y %Y -p %P -l %L'
# Without the binary, setup registers git's own text merge instead (./.fork/setup.sh
# --check then fails until mergiraf is installed: brew install mergiraf, then
# re-run setup). Full language list: mergiraf languages --gitattributes
# Lockfiles and generated files are regenerated, never merged (the !merge lines at the
# end pull lockfiles the globs capture back out). Add a line per lockfile or generated
# file the project has that a glob above captures.
*.rs    merge=mergiraf
*.ts    merge=mergiraf
*.tsx   merge=mergiraf
*.js    merge=mergiraf
*.jsx   merge=mergiraf
*.mjs   merge=mergiraf
*.cjs   merge=mergiraf
*.py    merge=mergiraf
*.go    merge=mergiraf
*.java  merge=mergiraf
*.rb    merge=mergiraf
*.kt    merge=mergiraf
*.kts   merge=mergiraf
*.php   merge=mergiraf
*.cs    merge=mergiraf
*.dart  merge=mergiraf
*.c     merge=mergiraf
*.h     merge=mergiraf
*.cc    merge=mergiraf
*.hh    merge=mergiraf
*.cpp   merge=mergiraf
*.hpp   merge=mergiraf
*.ex    merge=mergiraf
*.exs   merge=mergiraf
*.scala merge=mergiraf
*.sol   merge=mergiraf
# Declarative formats mergiraf merges structurally:
*.json  merge=mergiraf
*.yml   merge=mergiraf
*.yaml  merge=mergiraf
*.toml  merge=mergiraf
*.html  merge=mergiraf
*.xml   merge=mergiraf
*.ini   merge=mergiraf
*.properties merge=mergiraf
# Lockfiles the globs above would capture — regenerated, never merged:
package-lock.json   !merge
npm-shrinkwrap.json !merge
*-lock.yaml         !merge
*-lock.yml          !merge
*.lock.json         !merge
# The project's own merge lines go below this block (the last matching line wins).
# END superflow:fork
